; symmetric-power norm convergence and the occupation estimate are separately supplied. The raw nonsmooth sign output is outside this lemma until smoothed.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-classical-strong-limit"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.classical_strong_limit","kind":"claim","label":"Smooth local formulas converge strongly with occupation bounds","locator":"07-positive-temperature.tex:534–678; lem:classical-strong-limit, eq:classical-energy-transfer","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-positive","statement":"For a fixed smooth finite descendant calculation with polynomially bounded derivatives, leaves with all moments, centered finite-degree child columns and convergent finite coefficients, the embedded output converges in norm to its recursive Gaussian realization. A one-child replacement estimate of order 1/D and Efron–Stein give uniform first child occupation. For centered equivariant outputs, the root-shift energy therefore equals the scaled edge limit.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/circuit.classical_strong_limit","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/circuit.classical_strong_limit","id":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_strong_limit%22%2C%22circuit.energy_transfer%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_strong_limit%22%2C%22circuit.energy_transfer%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/circuit.energy_transfer"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/circuit.classical_strong_limit","id":"sha256:05cd